        "text": "Page: High Tider. Sentence: High Tider or \"Hoi Toider\" is a dialect of American English spoken in very limited communities of the South Atlantic United States—particularly, several small island and coastal townships of the rural North Carolina \"Down East\" seaside region that encompasses the Outer Banks and Pamlico Sound (specifically including Atlantic, Sea Level, and Harkers Island in eastern Carteret County, and also Ocracoke) as well as of the Chesapeake Bay (such as Tangier and Smith Island).\nPage: Tangier, Virginia. Sentence: Since 1850, the island's landmass has been reduced by 67%.",
